-- Explicit API-role privileges on schema public.
-- Newer hosted Supabase projects do NOT auto-grant table/sequence/function privileges to anon/authenticated/service_role
-- (classic projects, and the PGlite harness, do via default privileges). Without grants the Data API sees "permission
-- denied" even where RLS policies exist. This migration states the FINAL intended privilege state explicitly, so it is
-- identical on both kinds of project. It is a snapshot of the state produced by migrations 0001..0048 on a classic
-- project (table/column/sequence/function ACLs after every deliberate REVOKE/GRANT: column-level revokes, revoked
-- functions, append-only tables, service-role-only RPCs). packages/db/src/api_grants.test.ts proves equality.
-- Idempotent: each object is revoked from all API roles, then granted exactly. Storage/auth schemas are not touched.
-- Maintenance: objects created by LATER migrations still need their own explicit grants/revokes (default privileges
-- below give classic-style ALL to API roles on new objects, so new objects MUST revoke what they do not intend).

grant usage on schema public to anon, authenticated, service_role;

alter default privileges in schema public grant all on tables to anon, authenticated, service_role;
alter default privileges in schema public grant all on sequences to anon, authenticated, service_role;
alter default privileges in schema public grant all on functions to anon, authenticated, service_role;

